 "manifest": {
  "_id": "@apex-inc/mcp-server",
  "_rev": "57-152d0174b4f907a7cae19f61e049d3a2",
  "description": "MCP server for Apex. Your coding agent talks to the same Apex the dashboard uses.",
  "dist-tags": {
   "latest": "0.34.0"
  },
  "keywords": [
   "mcp",
   "apex"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "maintainers": [
   {
    "email": "[redacted-email:7efe3f612f75]",
    "name": "apex.inc"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@apex-inc/mcp-server",
  "readme": "# @apex-inc/mcp-server\n\nMCP server for Apex. Your coding agent talks to the same Apex the dashboard uses.\n\nDocs: [app.apex.inc/docs/mcp](https://app.apex.inc/docs/mcp/overview)\n\n## Install from Apex\n\n1. Open **Settings \u2192 AI Agents**.\n2. Leave **Device flow** selected.\n3. Click **Install in Cursor** or **Install in VS Code**.\n\nNo key goes in the file. The first Apex tool call prints an approval link.\n\n## Manual config\n\nAdd to `.cursor/mcp.json` (or your MCP client's equivalent). Those `npx` arguments are required.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"apex\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"-p\", \"@apex-inc/mcp-server\", \"mcp-server\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"APEX_URL\": \"https://app.apex.inc\",\n        \"APEX_WORKSPACE_KEY\": \"your-workspace-key\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFor a static key (CI, or a locked-down laptop), add `APEX_API_KEY` (`apex_uk_\u2026` or `apex_sk_\u2026`). Generate it on **Settings \u2192 AI Agents**.\n\n| Variable | Required | Notes |\n|----------|----------|-------|\n| `APEX_URL` | Yes | `https://app.apex.inc` in production. `http://localhost:3000` for local Apex. |\n| `APEX_WORKSPACE_KEY` | No | Shop this session starts on. `APEX_PROJECT_KEY` is the old name and still works. |\n| `APEX_API_KEY` | No | Omit when you use device flow. |\n\nThe editor Tools list is the live catalog. Do not treat a short list in a blog post as the count.\n\n## Screenshot CLI\n\nPlaywright runs on **their** machine, then the picture uploads. Apex cannot sign into their product.\n\n```bash\n# Experiment arm (public or localhost)\nnpx @apex-inc/mcp-server screenshot \\\n  --experiment <id> --variant control --url https://example.com --preview\n\n# Milestone still \u2014 signed-in product\nnpx playwright codegen --save-storage .apex/auth.json https://app.theirproduct.com\nnpx @apex-inc/mcp-server screenshot \\\n  --milestone <id> --state not_yet --url https://app.theirproduct.com/reports \\\n  --storage-state .apex/auth.json\nnpx @apex-inc/mcp-server screenshot \\\n  --milestone <id> --state done --url https://app.theirproduct.com/reports \\\n  --storage-state .apex/auth.json\n```\n\n`--storage-state` is a login file on this machine. Apex never receives it \u2014 only the picture. Install Playwright once: `npm i -D playwright && npx playwright install chromium`.\n\n## License\n\nMIT \u2014 see [LICENSE](./LICENSE)\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
